/**
 * "Chaotic Chatflow" — a deliberately nonsensical, deliberately GIGANTIC
 * chat-flow bundle whose only purpose is to exercise every node type,
 * attribute variation, edge variation, persona register and sub-flow
 * mechanic the Viglet Turing ES chat-flow engine supports, all at once.
 *
 * <p>It is authored with {@code @viglet/turing-flow-dsl} so the act of
 * building this fixture also exercises the DSL itself (transpile, bundle
 * cross-reference validation, the suspend node, functionCall/scheduleAgent
 * failure edges, and the enriched persona shape added alongside this file).
 * {@code transpileBundle(chaoticBundle)} is the single source of truth for
 * {@code turing-app/src/test/resources/harness-it/chaotic-chatflow.chat-flow.json},
 * regenerated by {@code scripts/emit-chaotic-fixture.mjs}.
 *
 * <h2>Theme</h2>
 * The Ministry of Absurd Chaos. None of it makes sense — that is the point.
 * What matters is the SHAPE:
 *
 * <h2>Deterministic golden path (main flow, walked by loadOrInitState with
 * a null aux model — NO LLM required)</h2>
 * <pre>
 *   start
 *   → persona(Herald)            __activePersonaId
 *   → slot SET chaos_key=alpha   (override)
 *   → writeSlot greeting="Hail {{chaos_key}} traveler"
 *   → condition chaos_key=='alpha'  (YES, both edges land on slot-marker)
 *   → slot SET marker=hit
 *   → condition chaos_key=='omega'  (NO branch taken)
 *   → slot SET second=from-no
 *   → switch chaos_key  (exact match → opt-alpha)
 *   → slot SET sw=exact
 *   → switch ghost_var  (missing var → wildcard fallback)
 *   → persona(Goblin)
 *   → subFlow chaos-sandwich  (descend: persona(Chef)+slot+writeSlot, then ascend)
 *   → slot DELETE marker
 *   → aiQuestion(chaos_key)  (already filled → skip-if-satisfied)
 *   → aiQuestion(quest_name) ← WALK STOPS HERE (first unfilled question)
 * </pre>
 * The remaining "tail" nodes (formCapture, validation rules, inlineOptions,
 * toolsEnabled/requiredTools, every onJudgeReject value, a colour switch,
 * a suspend gate, a subFlowSwitch into paperwork/ouroboros, and
 * functionCall/scheduleAgent finalizers) live AFTER the first unfilled
 * question, so they are covered structurally + by the LLM-gated walk, not
 * by the deterministic pass.
 *
 * @since 2026.3.1
 */
